# Append-only prose: when two branches add to it, keep both additions rather
# than stop the merge. Union is lossless (nothing is ever dropped) but it can
# duplicate a hunk both sides edited, so it is only ever safe on files a
# human reads and never on anything a parser does — JSON, code and lockfiles
# come out syntactically broken. scripts/repoMergePolicy.contract.test.js
# refuses anything but .md here.
#
# This file is touched by 4.3% of all commits (measured 2026-09-01), almost
# always to append an endpoint. That is the whole reason it is listed.
docs/_API-DOCUMENTATION.md merge=union
